case in the quiet apartment. She closes it, glances around, grabs her travel bag, and heads for the door. Preserve her identity, hairstyle, clothing, room layout, objects, and morning light.\n\nOff‑screen narration (use {{AUDIO_1}} for the entire video):\n\"They say leaving is the hardest part, but I think it's the first step that weighs the most..\"\n\nThe woman never speaks on screen; her lips remain naturally closed. Her expressions and actions convey the emotional weight of departure, travel, and arrival.\n\nDuring the first part of the narration, emphasize the farewell to the familiar apartment.\n\n[Shot 2] Transition naturally to the driving environment ({{IMAGE_2}}). The same woman drives away from the city – buildings shrink in the rear‑view mirror, roads open toward the countryside. Preserve her appearance, car interior, clothing, lighting, and composition from the reference. She drives silently, with focused expressions and realistic movements, while narration continues.\n\n[Shot 3] Transition naturally to {{IMAGE_3}}. The woman stands by the ocean with her travel bag nearby, then walks slowly toward the viewing area and gazes across the sea. Wind moves her hair and clothing. She remains silent, lips closed, as narration plays to the end. Camera starts behind her, then pulls backward with large amplitude, revealing the expansive coastline and sunset.\n\nCamera: Slow, cinematic, smooth, restrained – no abrupt cuts or exaggerated moves.\n\noverall_soundscape: Quiet apartment tone + suitcase sounds; then road/engine ambience; finally coastal wind and distant waves.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Minimal piano in apartment, gentle rhythmic texture on the road, warm sustained strings at the ocean. Music stays low enough to never overpower {{AUDIO_1}}."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "flags": {}, "type": "CR Text", "title": "提示词", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [400, 200], "